# Allow-list: the build context is exactly what `cargo build` and the image
# need. Everything else is either huge (target/ runs to gigabytes, .git/ to
# hundreds of megabytes) or has no business being sent to the daemon — a
# stray .env or local config can never leak into a layer this way.
*
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!src
!docker/config.toml
